...[pause=0.3][b]The doorbell rings.[/b]
[style name="bwuh"]
OW (neutral): Hello, is this the computer repair shop?
OW (sad): I'm sorry for coming in at such a late hour, I just got off work and this is the only time I have to come here...
MC (smile): Oh, that's alright. Thank you for coming.
MC (neutral_closed): (there goes my free time...)
MC (neutral): (but this man seems really tired, I should help him out)
OW (neutral): There seems to be a problem with my work laptop.
label diagnose_intro
- What's the issue?
	MC: What's the issue?
	OW (frown): Lately... whenever I try to get some work done on my laptop, I keep finding myself swamped by these notifications and ads.
	OW (sad): It has gotten so bad that I can't get anything done nowadays. That's when I overheard my co-workers talking about this place.
	MC (smile): Well, you're at the right place. I can get rid of those for you.
	OW (neutral): You have my utmost gratitude.
- Let me think for a moment.
	MC (neutral): (Let me hear him out first.)
	jump diagnose_intro
MC (neutral): Do you remember doing anything before this started? Like installing something?
OW (neutral): Hmm, let's see... there was a program that I had to install for work.
OW (neutral): After I started using it, I noticed a decrease in my laptop performance.
OW (frown): But I didn't think much of it, until there was an advertisement for a program that cleans the computer and makes it run faster.
OW (sad): I thought it'd be helpful, but it only got worse from then...
OW (sad): To top it off, the program deleted important work data.
MC (frown): That's awful! I'm sorry that happened to you.
label diagnose_choice
MC: (I see now, the problem is...)
- Bloatware
	jump diagnose_correct
- Malware
	MC (frown): (wait, that isn't quite right...)
	OW (neutral): Is there something wrong?
	set {Global.current_day_score} -= 20
	[signal arg="wrong_diagnosis"]
	if {Global.current_day_score} <= 0:
		jump diagnose_failed
	jump diagnose_choice
- System Failure
	MC (frown): (wait, that isn't quite right...)
